                    response: I propose fine-tuning a                           
                    pretrained MobileNetV2 from timm with                       
                    a single-output head and using                              
                    per-sample weights based on inverse                         
                    skin-tone frequencies in the loss to                        
                    improve fairness. We perform 5-fold                         
                    stratified CV on the binary malignant                       
                    label with standard augmentations,                          
                    computing a weighted BCE loss and                           
                    reporting mean AUROC. After CV                              
                    evaluation, we retrain on the full                          
                    dataset and save the final model. A                         
                    `predict()` function loads the saved                        
                    model and returns malignancy                                
